# D23 (LOAD-BEARING, invariant #8 — the WORST pre-D23 mode): a `throws` EQUIP
# METHOD call in an unhandled position. Pre-D23 `s.risky()` typed as bare `int`
# (throws-ness dropped entirely), so `int x = 1 + s.risky()` PASSED `gg check`
# and produced GARBAGE at runtime (measured `x=281473914366657`) — a silent
# miscompile from safe code. Now it must REJECT with E_UnhandledThrows.
struct S:
    int v

equip S:
    int risky(self) throws String:
        if self.v > 0:
            throw "boom"
        return 5

void main():
    S s = S(3)
    int x = 1 + s.risky()
    print(x)
